t me wri[0m[7B[3A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[20A[16B[50C[38;2;124;124;124mte the p[2B[0m[38;2;255;215;135m⠸⠀[0m[5B[3A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[20A[J[38;2;124;124;124mThe problem asks to compute the conditional probability $P(\inf_{t\in[1,2]} W_t [0m[38;2;124;124;124m< 0 \mid W_1 > 0, W_2 > 0)$ for standard Brownian motion.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFirst, let me set up the problem. We have standard Brownian motion $W_t$. We [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcondition on $W_1 > 0$ and $W_2 > 0$. We want the probability that the infimum [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mon $[1,2]$ is negative, i.e., the process goes below 0 at some point in $[1,2]$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mLet me use the Markov property. Condition on $W_1 = x > 0$. Then on $[1,2]$, the[0m[38;2;124;124;124mprocess is $x + (W_t - W_1)$ for $t \in [1,2]$, which is $x + B_s$ where $B_s = [0m[38;2;124;124;124mW_{1+s} - W_1$ is a Brownian motion for $s \in [0,1]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $\inf_{t \in [1,2]} W_t = x + \inf_{s \in [0,1]} B_s$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe want $P(\inf_{t \in [1,2]} W_t < 0 \mid W_1 = x, W_2 > 0) = P(x + \inf_{s \in[0m[38;2;124;124;124m[0,1]} B_s < 0 \mid B_1 > -x)$... [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, $W_2 = W_1 + (W_2 - W_1) = x + B_1$. So $W_2 > 0$ means $B_1 > -x$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo we need $P(\inf_{s \in [0,1]} B_s < -x \mid B_1 > -x)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBy the reflection principle, for a Brownian motion $B_s$ on $[0,1]$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$P(\inf_{s \in [0,1]} B_s < -x \mid B_1 = y) = \exp(-2x(x+y)/1) \text{ for } y [0m[38;2;124;124;124m> -x$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, let me recall the reflection principle more carefully. For Brownian motion[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$B_t$ on $[0,T]$, the joint density of $(B_T, \inf_{0 \le s \le T} B_s)$ is:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor $m < 0$ and $m \le y$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$P(B_T \in dy, \inf_{0 \le s \le T} B_s \ge m) = \left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi T}} [0m[38;2;124;124;124me^{-y^2/(2T)} - \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi T}} e^{-(y-2m)^2/(2T)}\right] dy$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $P(B_T \in dy, \inf B_s \ge -x) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}} \left[e^{-y^2/2} - [0m
[38;2;124;124;124me^{-(y+2x)^2/2}\right] dy$ for $T=1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAnd $P(B_T \in dy) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}} e^{-y^2/2} dy$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $P(\inf B_s \ge -x \mid B_1 = y) = 1 - e^{-(y+2x)^2/2 + y^2/2} = 1 - e^{-(y^2[0m[38;2;124;124;124m+ 4xy + 4x^2 - y^2)/2} = 1 - e^{-(4xy + 4x^2)/2} = 1 - e^{-2x(y+x)}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is valid for $y > -x$ (so that $y + x > 0$, making the exponent negative [0m
